## TL;DR

```bash
cd <repo-root>
bash tools/scratch/compose-domain/{{RUN_ID}}/graduate.sh
# follow the smoke instructions printed at the end
```

The script is **idempotent** — re-running is a no-op. If anything goes
wrong mid-run, it aborts loudly. Rollback at the end of this doc.

## What graduate.sh does

| # | Step | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Validate prereqs | (read-only) |
| 2 | Copy sandbox files | `api/server/skills/`, `api/server/personae/`, `api/server/mcp_tools/`, `api/functions/workflows/`, `api/functions/graphs/`, `api/functions/graphs/executors/agents/`, `api/functions/graphs/executors/validators/` |
| 3 | Patch `function_app.py` | Adds orchestrator + activity decorators, between BEGIN/END markers |
| 4 | Patch `api/functions/graphs/__init__.py` | Adds `build_*_workflow` exports |
| 5 | Patch `api/server/services/simulator_orchestrator.py` | Adds `spawn_{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_workflow`; adds `{{WORKFLOW_TYPE}}` to `ramp_loop`'s `spawners` dict |
| 6 | Patch `api/server/routes/simulator.py` | Adds `POST /api/simulator/{{DOMAIN_NAME}}` |
| 7 | Patch `api/server/services/blueprint_inventory.py` | Adds DOMAINS entry with `workflow_type` + `phase_aliases` |
| 8 | Patch `api/shared/constants.py` | Lifts `<PHASE>_TIMEOUT` constants out of orchestrator |
| 9 | Print smoke commands + expected event sequence | (read-only) |

Each patch step is idempotent: it checks for a unique anchor before
appending, so re-running graduate.sh is safe.

