## Recording for replay

After smoke passes, record real walks so the deployed page replays them:

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:3101/api/blueprint/_recorder/start
sleep 300                                              # ~3 walks per domain
curl -X POST http://localhost:3101/api/blueprint/_recorder/stop

# Inspect; prune partial / single-event noise files; commit.
ls -la data/blueprint-recordings/{{WORKFLOW_TYPE}}-*.jsonl
find data/blueprint-recordings -name '*.jsonl' -size -200c -delete
git add data/blueprint-recordings/{{WORKFLOW_TYPE}}-*.jsonl
git commit -m 'record(blueprint): real walks for {{DOMAIN_DISPLAY_NAME}}'

# Redeploy.
./scripts/deploy-blueprint.sh
```

## Rollback (if smoke fails)

The bug is in a SKILL.md (compose-domain or one of the sub-skills),
not in the graduated code. Revert the graduation, fix the SKILL.md,
re-run compose-domain, re-graduate.

```bash
# Revert all the file patches.
git checkout -- \
    function_app.py \
    api/functions/graphs/__init__.py \
    api/server/services/simulator_orchestrator.py \
    api/server/routes/simulator.py \
    api/server/services/blueprint_inventory.py \
    api/shared/constants.py

# Remove all the copied files.
rm -rf \
    api/server/skills/{{DOMAIN_NAME}}-* \
    api/server/personae/{{PERSONA_ROLES_SPACED}} \
    api/functions/workflows/{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}.py \
    api/functions/workflows/{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_activities.py \
    api/functions/graphs/{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_*.py \
    api/functions/graphs/executors/agents/agent_{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_*.py \
    api/functions/graphs/executors/validators/validate_{{DOMAIN_NAME_SNAKE}}_*.py
{{REMOVE_NEW_TOOLS_BLOCK}}
```

Then: fix the offending SKILL.md, delete the sandbox, re-invoke
compose-domain, re-graduate.
